Lujvo and cmene are mutually exclusive classes of words, each with its own
distinctive structure. The defining characteristic of cmene is that cmene
and only cmene end in a consonant. Even a cmene that appears to be a lujvo
with an extra consonant on the end is only a cmene; it lost it's lujvo
status when the consonant was added.
While lujvo can always be decomposed into components (that's the whole poin=
t
of lujvo), cmene can never be decomposed into components, although they are
often (and deliberately) suggestive of such components.

stevo

